# {{ title }}

A multi-tenant Navree app, started from the `{{ kit }}` starter kit: sign-up
with email verification, two-factor sign-in, social sign-in, workspaces with
members, roles and invitations, billing per workspace, settings, an admin
panel at `/admin`, and an example feature (projects){% if web %}, with a Next.js
and shadcn/ui front end in `web/`{% endif %}.

## Getting started

You need Rust, the `navree` CLI and Docker or Podman{% if web %}, plus Node.js 22 and
pnpm for the front end{% endif %}.

```sh
navree dock up                 # {{ database_name }} and Mailpit (http://localhost:8025)
navree key:generate            # then set APP_KEY in .env
navree migrate:fresh --seed    # tables and a demo workspace
{% if web %}
pnpm --dir web install         # the web app's packages
navree dev                     # API on :8080, web app on http://localhost:3000
{% else %}
navree dev                     # API on http://127.0.0.1:8080, reference at /api/docs
{% endif %}
```

Sign in as `owner@{{ package | replace("_", "-") }}.test` (password `password123`); the owner is
also a super admin, so the admin panel at {% if web %}http://localhost:3000/admin{% else %}http://127.0.0.1:8080/admin{% endif %} opens
for them. `member@{{ package | replace("_", "-") }}.test` is a member of the same workspace.

## What's where

| Path | What it holds |
|---|---|
| `src/platform.rs` | The framework modules: auth, access, workspaces, billing, social sign-in, real time, Helm, ... |
| `src/modules/accounts/` | Sessions and the sign-in options (`/api/v1/account`) |
| `src/modules/settings/` | Workspace name and slug, notification preferences, workspace billing |
| `src/modules/projects/` | The example feature: copy it for your own |
| `src/modules/admin/` | The admin panel's resources |
| `src/abilities.rs` | Ability rules; role permissions are in `config/app.toml` |
| `src/seed.rs` | The demo workspace |
{% if web %}
| `web/` | The Next.js front end and its backend-for-frontend |
{% endif %}

## Billing

`billing.provider = "fake"` in `config/app.toml` lets you click through
checkout without a payment account. For production, set
`APP_BILLING__PROVIDER=stripe` (or `paddle`), put the keys in the
environment (`APP_BILLING__STRIPE__SECRET_KEY`,
`APP_BILLING__STRIPE__WEBHOOK_SECRET`), and set each plan's price ids
under `[billing.plans.*]`.

## The API contract

`openapi.json` is the OpenAPI document, committed. After changing a route
or a DTO, run `navree openapi:export openapi.json` to write it again; the
CI workflow fails when the committed file no longer matches the code.
{% if web %}
`pnpm --dir web gen:api` does both: it exports the document and
regenerates the web app's types in `web/lib/api/schema.d.ts`.
{% endif %}

